### Phase 5 — Kafka notifications

There is no Notification HTTP API on the Gateway. Confirm a booking / place an order, then watch **notification-service** logs for:

`Email notification sent to customer ...`

Start Kafka first:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.kafka.yml up -d
```

### Confirm booking (CUSTOMER token) — publishes stayfinder.booking-confirmed
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/1/confirm
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### Mock payment confirm — same event
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/1/payment/confirm
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### Place food order (booking must already be CONFIRMED) — publishes stayfinder.food-order-placed
POST http://localhost:8080/api/food/orders
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hotelId": 1,
  "bookingId": 1,
  "roomNumber": "101",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Notification has no public business API
GET http://localhost:8084/actuator/health

GET http://localhost:8084/api/notifications
# expect 403

GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications
# expect 404 at Gateway — no route
